  Status: author draft; independent mathematical and source-correspondence
  review pending. Pinned source revision:
  <verbatim|3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464>.

  <section|Scope><label|scope>

  The manuscript is <verbatim|manuscript/existence/centered-geometry-producer.tex>.
  It proves the opened-copy construction of the migration, occupancy, and
  separated-origin inputs needed by the finite-volume centered moment route.
  It does not produce marched weights, paid response estimates, the terminal
  service receipt, or vacuum prices.

  <section|Correspondence><label|correspondence>

  <block|<tformat|<twith|table-width|1par>|<twith|table-hmode|exact>|<cwith|1|-1|1|-1|cell-hyphen|t>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-bborder|1ln>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-valign|bottom>|<table|<row|<cell|<strong|Assertion>>|<cell|<strong|Pinned
  declarations / files>>|<cell|<strong|Inspection notes>>>|<row|<cell|Open
  schedule and aligned sublattice>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Stock.Tabs.opens>,
  <verbatim|.open_later>; <verbatim|YM.Cells.center>,
  <verbatim|YM.Cells.Mix.camp>, <verbatim|YM.Cells.copy_home>;
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Overlay/Prior.lean>, <verbatim|Lean/YM/Cells/*>>|<cell|The
  source defines <verbatim|Tabs.opens i j> by <verbatim|i\<leq\>j> and
  <verbatim|s * coverSize(j)^2 \<leq\> a_i/a_j>. <verbatim|Tabs.open_later>
  propagates this opening to later levels using
  <verbatim|coverSize(j+1)^2\<leq\>2 coverSize(j)^2> and block ratio at least
  3. At parameter one the initial bound is <verbatim|B_k^2\<leq\>a_m/a_k>;
  exact adjacent ratios then inductively give <verbatim|B_j^2\<leq\>a_m/a_j>.
  Adjacent integer side ratios compose exactly, and <verbatim|camp> is the
  canonical ratio embedding after the opening.>>|<row|<cell|Ratio embeddings
  compose and preserve ancestry>|<cell|Private <verbatim|embed_comp> and
  <verbatim|YM.Work.I03.camp_step>; <verbatim|Lean/YM/Work/I03.lean>>|<cell|Exact
  divisibility identifies the composite ratio count with the product of
  adjacent counts, so the canonical embeddings agree. The resulting step
  identity gives <verbatim|embed_j(o_j(x))=o_{j+1}(x)>, equivalently
  <verbatim|parent(o_{j+1}(x))=o_j(x)>.>>|<row|<cell|Separation and
  injectivity>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Work.I03.answer>;
  <verbatim|YM.Corona.below>; <verbatim|Lean/YM/Work/I03.lean>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Corona/Spend.lean>>|<cell|Distinct coarse sites have max
  periodic separation at least one. In each coordinate choose a centered
  integer representative of the difference; multiplying it by the exact ratio
  keeps it centered in the larger periodic side, including half-side ties.
  Thus the max periodic separation scales by exactly the integer ratio, and
  the opening induction gives <verbatim|B_j^2\<leq\>sep(o_j(x),o_j(y))>.
  Positivity of the right side makes the copy map injective. This is the
  arithmetic proved by <verbatim|Corona.below>.>>|<row|<cell|Terminal copy
  identity>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Bid.I03.ticket>;
  <verbatim|YM.Work.I03.answer>; <verbatim|copy_home>;
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Bid/Fuels.lean>, <verbatim|Lean/YM/Work/I03.lean>, and
  cell construction dependencies>|<cell|The ticket's first field identifies
  the centered root copy map with <verbatim|camp> at the terminal level.
  <verbatim|camp> is the same aligned embedding used in the
  manuscript.>>|<row|<cell|Occupancy and geometric input to the public moment
  route>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Extra.Multi.Occupancy.of_injective>;
  <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Accent.tentF>; <verbatim|Lean/YM/Extra/MULTISOURCE_BOUNDS/Root.lean>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/FullVolume/Dusk/Tackle.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|tentF> uses
  the root sites as the finite name set, obtains injectivity from the
  copy-spacing field, and converts it to occupancy at most one. Its
  hypothesis <verbatim|1\<leq\>r_j> upgrades that to the requested occupancy
  bound. The same separation field is packaged as the <verbatim|Drake> input
  at the opened scale.>>>>>

  <section|Public consumer and limits><label|public-consumer-and-limits>

  The selected root-test consumer <verbatim|Accent.tentF> builds the site
  family by centering a single root cell and taking its copy names. The
  source calls the geometric interface with opening parameter one, derives
  spacing by <verbatim|I03>, uses injectivity for occupancy, and passes
  migration/occupancy/Drake into <verbatim|Accent.occursT>. The downstream
  multiscale propagation of those geometric facts under Brine weights is
  separately proved in the centered-construction chapter. The remaining
  independent inputs to that consumer are the selected weight/paid-size,
  service, and vacuum-price data.

  <section|Checks><label|checks>

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item>Inspected only the declarations and immediate dependencies listed
    above; no Lean source was changed and no Lean build was run.

    <item>The combined wrapper <verbatim|/tmp/ym-centered-fragment.tex>
    compiled successfully with <verbatim|latexmk -pdf
    -interaction=nonstopmode -halt-on-error
    -outdir=/tmp/ym-centered-fragment-build /tmp/ym-centered-fragment.tex>,
    producing 36 pages. Pages 35\U36 were rendered and inspected; page 35
    contains the end of the two-page geometry lemma. The wrapper has 11
    unresolved references from omitted OPE, lattice rate/step, and
    column-subpower units.

    <item>No literature reference applies to this project-specific lattice
    embedding argument.
  </itemize-minus>

